# gate/layering.rules — forbidden dependency directions.
#
# Layers are ordered TOKEN -> AST -> SEMA -> IR -> BACKEND. A layer may depend
# upward (a backend may read IR; sema may read the AST). Downward reaches are
# what this file forbids, because a downward reach is a layer recovering by
# hand something the layer above it was supposed to hand over.
#
# THE ONE THAT MOTIVATES THE FILE: a backend that imports AST or Sema is not
# consuming a decided answer, it is re-deriving meaning at emission time. That
# is where a "the compiler is wrong" diagnosis comes from -- two places decide
# the same thing and disagree.
#
# IR IS DELIBERATELY NOT SEMA. `types.zig` and `native_ir.zig` are the settled
# contract handed to a backend. A backend reading them is reading an answer.
# See gate/layers.manifest.
#
# FORMAT: <from-layer> <to-layer>

BACKEND AST
BACKEND SEMA
AST     SEMA
AST     BACKEND
IR      AST
IR      SEMA
IR      BACKEND
SEMA    BACKEND
TOKEN   AST
TOKEN   SEMA
TOKEN   IR
TOKEN   BACKEND
